<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml), its spider mine module left off; a field not
    discussed here is the Controller's. Plating, the research gate, the absent apparel tags
    and the unmasked art follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: the set's command piece.
    - MechControlGroups 1, Biotech's control pack's.
    - HackingSpeed 0.2 for the hacking the overlord trait leaves the pilot. No vanilla apparel
      carries the stat.
    - No MechBandwidth: the helmet's 12 and the armor's 8 are the set's.
    - costList: ComponentSpacer 2 / Plasteel 60 is the Controller shoulders' price, the
      plasteel about 0.4 of the armor's as across the tier. SignalChip 2 is the price of
      Biotech's bandwidth pack, so the command range has a price and the set's chips climb
      from the diabolus's here through the war queen's on the helmet to the apocriton's on
      the armor.

    Command range: the CommandRangeExtension lets a mechanitor wearing the pads order drafted
    mechs anywhere on the map they share (scope CurrentMap), where vanilla stops every order
    at 24.9 cells from the overseer. radius is the Radius scope's reach and the settings
    slider's default, vanilla's 24.9 so that switching to that scope starts from vanilla.
    normalRadius, unset here and so vanilla's, is the range without the set; a mod that moves
    the range for everyone has both written by its compat root
    (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/CommandRange.xml). The settings overwrite the entry and
    may move it to the helmet; Source/1.6/CommandRange/CommandRange.cs has the rules and the
    vanilla call paths.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor's header; Merge still ORs the
    base's isUnifiedApparel in.

    Patched by the 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root alone, which restates the piece on
    CE's scale; see its headers.

    Draw order: drawData's south offset 0.014 puts the pads under the helmet facing south, as
    the art wants. A worn apparel node's altitude is its drawData offset y (added verbatim by
    PawnRenderTree.TryGetMatrix) plus PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer(layer), 0.000366 per
    layer unit, the layer being the parent's base (ApparelBody 20, ApparelHead 70) plus the
    piece's index among that parent's apparel; the y offsets on VFEP's bases are what order
    the pieces. The base's 0.02 lands at 0.027 to 0.028, just over the helmets' 0.027; 0.014
    lands at 0.021 to 0.022, at least 0.004 under any helmet and 0.003 over the shell (0.017
    to 0.018), above post-apparel wounds (layer 30, 0.011) and firefoam (40, 0.015); hair
    and beard (about 0.022) can draw over the pads on a bare head. Only this piece moves, so
    every helmet and armor, ours or VFEP's, keeps its altitude and foundry mixes stay
    consistent. North, east and west inherit the base's 0.2, 0.02 and 0.02
    (XmlInheritance merges same-named elements recursively, so only the changed facing is
    listed); the north 0.2 and the armor's 0.1 are what the cerebrex node is slotted between
    (1.6/Mods/Odyssey/Patches/CerebrexNodeDrawOrder.xml), so a north offset on either piece
    moves against that patch's 0.134.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketShoulders_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, equipped with command relays that let the pilot order mechs anywhere on the map.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, equipped with command relays that let the pilot order mechs anywhere on the map.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The resurrector in the shell holds a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for whichever mechs are needed most at the time. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, and the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordShoulders</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechControlGroups>1</MechControlGroups>
      <HackingSpeed>0.2</HackingSpeed>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
      <SignalChip>2</SignalChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <!-- Under the helmet facing south; see "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataSouth><offset>(0, 0.014, 0)</offset></dataSouth>
      </drawData>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CommandRangeExtension">
        <scope>CurrentMap</scope>
        <radius>24.9</radius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
